From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:59:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 097/148] hjviewer: iOS speaks Korean, the splash takes the
 home's colours, phone settings start with language

UX-M1:
- U66: CFBundleLocalizations ko and en, ko in the project's knownRegions, and ko.lproj and
  en.lproj InfoPlist.strings for the camera, photo library, Face ID (W13's text kept) and the
  local network (new, for direct connections to PCs on the same network). The English texts in
  Info.plist say what HJViewer uses them for.
- U70: the Android and iOS splash take the home's canvas (light) and surface (dark) and the
  tertiary text colour of 1.7.0's palette, so the first frame does not change the background.
- U40: the phone settings go account, app lock, settings (language, theme, keep awake, note),
  display, "Network (advanced)", then the rest. The server, proxy, WebSocket, TLS fallback, UDP,
  hole punching, IPv6 and WebRTC rows move to that sub-screen under the same conditions; it is
  left out when none of them shows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
